## 🚀 Getting Started

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Byteflux2002/Greenhouse-AgriRobot.git
cd Greenhouse-AgriRobot
```

### 2. Set Up the Backend
Open a terminal in the project root:

```bash
python -m venv .venv
```

Activate the virtual environment on Windows:

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

Install the backend dependencies listed in the project's requirements file, if available. If no requirements file exists, create one from the actual Python dependencies used by `Backend/app.py`.

Start the Flask application using the project's configured entry point. For example:

```powershell
python Backend/app.py
```

The backend address and port depend on the Flask configuration.

### 3. Set Up the Dashboard
Open a separate terminal:

```bash
cd Dashboard
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open the local URL printed by Vite in the terminal.

### 4. Connect the Hardware
- Upload the appropriate firmware to the Arduino UNO using Arduino IDE.
- Connect the ESP8266 and sensors according to the actual circuit diagram.
- Configure the backend and dashboard to use the correct communication endpoint.
- Verify sensor readings and pump-control behaviour before running the system unattended.

